WEBVTT

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:15.940
<i>Announce the resolutions you've made as the new president.</i>

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:17.330
<i>Oh, should I?</i>

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:23.750
<i>Now that I'm the president,</i>

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.750
<i>I'd like to participate in the Comifes as a circle.</i>

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:37.650
Oh, this is Sasahara.
Can you talk right now?

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:38.850
Well...

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:56.710
Look, we won the Comifes drawing.

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:03.570
Are you serious?

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:06.080
Are we in?

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.080
I said we won, didn't I?

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.000
Is that so!

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:14.230
What a half-hearted reaction.

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:15.260
Don't you want to go?

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.470
Of course I do.

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:20.850
How should I say it? I feel like Amuro did
right before his first battle against a Zaku.

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.970
<i>I won't let you!</i>

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:23.560
You must destroy it.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:25.430
<i>I didn't want to accept it.</i>

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:28.500
Well, in his case, he had two suits from the start.

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:30.360
We're not Newtypes anyway.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.660
You're not making any sense.

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:34.280
Where did they put us?

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:37.240
Here on Day 3.

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:40.010
Right in the middle of the island, as expected.

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:41.360
Well, of course.

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:42.580
Did you tell Kugayama?

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:45.000
Yes, I called him on his cell phone.

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:50.840
"O-Oh, I g-guess we r-really have to make the book now,"

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:51.900
he said.

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:58.640
We'll probably use some material from here, so it shouldn't be too much trouble.

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:00.580
Oh, you're rather prepared.

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:01.970
Of course.

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:03.780
I bet he drew a lot of those by now,

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:05.080
those erotic illustrations.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:08.190
Yeah, I think we'll be able to adapt many of them.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:10.740
Which ones should we use?

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:18.440
Is the book going to feature the president?

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:21.910
Well, there are a lot of drawings of her with Yamada,

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:23.480
like this one.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:26.580
Hey, doesn't this look better than usual?

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:31.150
Yeah, it looks better than what we saw in his room.

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:33.300
It seems like he becomes more enthusiastic about it as the scenes get more detailed.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.090
It's what you'd call human nature.

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:39.260
Well, from a practical standpoint, it's pretty usable.

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:43.350
In other words, it'll probably sell well.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.520
It really might!

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:54.090
H-Hey, Ogiue-san.

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:56.530
Hello.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:59.900
What brings you here at this time of day?

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:00.620
What happened to class?

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:02.270
It's been canceled.

00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:03.560
I see.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:05.570
What's going to sell well?

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:08.460
Well, you know...

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:09.470
Know what?

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:11.670
We won the drawing for the Comifes,

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:14.960
so we were going over an estimate of everything.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:19.550
Yeah, we were thinking about making a doujinshi.

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:20.590
Doujinshi...

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:24.460
We'd like you to help us out as much as possible, Ogiue-san.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:27.990
Are you not interested?

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:29.270
No, I don't mind.

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:33.080
Oh, this is the coveted circle ticket, isn't it?

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:34.780
There are only three, though.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:36.210
How should we distribute them?

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:37.320
Discuss that in a civilized manner.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:41.580
The entrance time for circle vendors is between 7:30 and 9:00.

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:45.530
Are the members lining up in the queue on a completely different schedule?

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:47.590
Most likely.

00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:49.970
The timetable's really complicated.

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:54.440
The times of commencement, intermission, and restart for courier parcel receipt acquisition have been set.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:57.020
What do they mean by
"register on behalf of your circle at any time"?

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:59.900
Do we have to go somewhere else just to do that?

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:04.340
Participation as a circle really is different from attending as an individual.

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:06.850
We need to read this thoroughly.

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:10.140
Sasahara.

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:12.100
Yes?

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:14.690
It seems like she wants our attention.

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:27.950
Did you draw that, Ogiue-san?

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:30.850
Oh, yes, sort of.

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:32.120
Mind if I take a look?

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:33.500
Well, I'm writing on the club's notebook, after all.

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:37.500
<i>Wow, she's pretty good.</i>

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:39.720
<i>Quite modern, I'd say.</i>

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:42.190
Why don't you have her draw something?

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:45.470
It'd be appropriate for a doujinshi to feature contributions from a number of people.

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:48.470
This is a Kujiun erotic spin-off, you know.

00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:51.580
Oh, that's fine. I don't mind.

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:53.780
Is that a problem?

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:54.440
Not at all.

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:57.360
Is it okay if I ask you to do it?

00:04:57.570 --> 00:04:58.430
Sure.

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:01.420
Can you draw one to two pages of illustrations?

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:04.200
I mean... you can draw
as much as you'd like.

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:06.980
Well, I can't draw that many.

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:09.240
Okay, sketches are fine for the time being.

00:05:09.860 --> 00:05:11.660
Okay, I'll do that for the time being.

00:05:12.070 --> 00:05:14.690
What are you going to do about the printing company?

00:05:14.690 --> 00:05:17.330
I'll ask Takayanagi-san for now.

00:05:18.140 --> 00:05:21.590
<i>It's the Comifes! We're going
to make a doujinshi!</i>

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:23.650
<i>Amazing!</i>

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:32.820
<i>This is what a college circle is all about. It's the real thing!</i>

00:05:33.570 --> 00:05:35.780
How many copies should we print?

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:40.340
I don't want leftovers, but I don't think we'll sell out.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:44.070
It's better to keep your hopes low.

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:46.250
Hi!

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:47.320
Hello!

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:48.120
Nyoro.

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:49.570
Oh, did you guys come here together?

00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:52.390
Well, we all just met outside.

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:56.460
Yeah, I just happened to catch Kuchiki-kun and Tanaka-san at the door.

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:01.330
Oh, Comifes!

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:04.340
Wow!

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:08.470
Is that the result of the drawing?
How'd it go?

00:06:08.810 --> 00:06:09.760
We made it.

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:11.660
Wow, that's great.

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:13.880
Is this the start of the first production meeting?

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:15.020
Not really.

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:17.900
What are you going to do about
the page count and the cover price?

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:20.350
This is the platinum ticket, isn't it?

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:23.040
I haven't decided anything at all.

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:25.910
I'd rather sell everything than pursue a profit.

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:27.880
Oh, I see.

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:32.710
Should I be a cosplay vendor?

00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:35.020
Would you be okay with doing that?

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:39.540
Cosplaying as a vendor is fine as long as we don't wield long objects.

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:44.310
Not that. What we're doing will be targeted at men, so wouldn't that be asking for sexual harassment?

00:06:45.350 --> 00:06:47.230
I don't mind at all.

00:06:47.230 --> 00:06:50.370
The customers might feel uneasy.

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:52.050
There's nothing to worry about.

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:54.520
Girls these days really are tough.

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:55.980
Ogiue-san included.

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:57.970
What do you mean?

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:02.460
We were thinking about having Ogiue-san draw a few pages.

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:06.660
Are you finally coming out?

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:08.610
Sen x Mugi or Mugi x Kabu?

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:11.530
It sounds like an insult when you put it as "coming out".

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:16.540
Well, most of it will be Kugayama-san's illustrations,
so males will be our target audience.

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:19.310
In that case, let's go with the president and vice president.

00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:22.180
Is the pairing the only thing you can think of?

00:07:22.180 --> 00:07:23.400
This is why...

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:30.300
Well, once we finalize our editing policy, I'd appreciate it if we stayed along those lines, I think.

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:33.920
Even though you've been elected
as the next student council's officers,

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:37.880
you are to obey the orders of the current student council.

00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:40.270
That's the rule of Rikkyouin Academy.

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:44.490
When it comes to Ogiue-san, you sure are quick to react, Ohno-san.

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:46.400
That wasn't me.

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:48.490
It was the spirit of the vice president speaking through me.

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:55.780
I was thinking about making a ceremony version anyway,
so the timing couldn't be better.

00:07:57.030 --> 00:08:01.030
Oh, Kisaragi Kasumi, what a wonderful outfit!

00:08:01.030 --> 00:08:05.220
Madam Ohno's vice president is second to none!

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:10.010
Sorry, I'll try to make some time for the stitching.

00:08:10.350 --> 00:08:12.540
You don't have to go out of your way for my sake.

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:14.180
If worst comes to worst, I can push myself a little more.

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:17.260
What a waste of talent and ability.

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:19.520
There's no such thing as a waste in cosplay!

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:23.180
If you're going to call that a waste, you could say the same thing about the entire doujin scene.

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:26.060
Right, and that's what people
refer to as culture.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:28.990
What a great way to end this conversation.

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:31.340
What about the day of the event?

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:33.030
About the vendors.

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:40.200
Tanaka-san and I will have to change before we arrive, so the earliest we can be there is around eleven.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:42.360
No problem.

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:45.420
Our policy is to do what we can.

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:47.940
Hey.

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:49.940
I heard you're going to participate in the manga festival.

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:51.260
Congratulations.

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:56.220
I'm going to be the vice president,
so you can be the president, Saki-san.

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:57.430
What are you talking about?

00:08:57.430 --> 00:08:59.190
I'm talking about cosplay.

00:08:59.190 --> 00:09:01.100
Co-s-pl-ay!

00:09:02.420 --> 00:09:05.100
You don't need to syllabify it, and don't decide things on your own.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:08.560
Why don't you do it, Ogippe?

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:10.720
Ogippe?

00:09:11.890 --> 00:09:13.140
I refuse.

00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:15.780
Has the layout been decided?

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:23.700
Well, I'm still unsure about whether we should decide on the number of pages now or talk about it later.

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:24.920
What did Kugayama-san say?

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:26.220
He said he'd leave it to us.

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:29.220
That's just like Kugapii.

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:30.380
Is he really that passive with his life?

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:33.210
I suppose he's just busy with job interviews.

00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:36.130
Can he do both? It must be hard.

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:37.470
I think so.

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:39.260
I doubt it.

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:43.220
Why do you have to be so pessimistic, Kasukabe-san?

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:47.150
Well, there's nothing more interesting than some drama in life.

00:09:47.610 --> 00:09:49.470
You make it sound as if this doesn't concern you.

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:59.290
We use Minami Printing, but it's a matter of preference.

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:04.670
Some people who make individual books don't like Minami because their coloring isn't great, but it's up to you.

00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:11.740
As you probably know, the surcharge increases as Comifes approaches.

00:10:11.740 --> 00:10:13.520
Have you finalized your plans?

00:10:13.520 --> 00:10:15.300
No, we still need to decide everything.

00:10:15.770 --> 00:10:17.150
Are you going to split expenses between members?

00:10:17.150 --> 00:10:18.330
That's what I was thinking.

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:21.260
Well, I don't think Kasukabe-san will pay her share, though.

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:26.250
Yeah, she's the type of character who'd probably ask, "Why do I have to pay?"

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:27.620
Right.

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:29.670
How's Ogiue-san?

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:32.550
How...? She's doing fine.

00:10:32.550 --> 00:10:33.840
Is she getting along?

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:38.320
If you asked me with a straight face, I wouldn't know what to say, but...

00:10:39.170 --> 00:10:40.840
Yes, she's doing fine.

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:42.000
I see.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:44.790
I'm thinking about having her draw something for us.

00:10:45.190 --> 00:10:49.000
Well, it's more accurate to say she wanted to do it.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:50.190
Oh, really?

00:10:51.010 --> 00:10:55.130
Our female members aren't going to participate this year.

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:58.190
Does the Manga Club have separate booths for guys and girls?

00:10:59.070 --> 00:11:02.830
Well, in the past two to three years, the girls are the ones who've had the momentum.

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:05.220
They're more focused on what they want to work on,

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:08.720
like Gangaru BLEED and Reass Mood.

00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:12.690
Males and females have different tastes, after all.

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:15.810
Student manga usually doesn't sell,
so we exhibit as separate contingents.

00:11:15.810 --> 00:11:18.320
The entire Manga Club publishes a doujinshi every other year.

00:11:19.550 --> 00:11:22.870
I see. Ogiue-san's participating...

00:11:22.870 --> 00:11:25.200
I suppose participating isn't the right term.

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:26.580
Is there a problem with that?

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:29.040
No, it's not a problem,

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:32.790
but you know how girls think.

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:36.450
That doesn't concern Ogiue-san at all, though.

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:40.490
You're right. You're absolutely right.

00:11:41.980 --> 00:11:46.660
I get the feeling I shouldn't be telling anybody about this.

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:48.520
Y-Yeah, you're right.

00:11:49.110 --> 00:11:52.510
Did you tell anyone else about winning the Comifes drawing?

00:11:52.510 --> 00:11:53.800
Anyone else?

00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:55.560
Excluding Genshiken members.

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:58.070
No, not yet.

00:11:58.970 --> 00:12:01.380
It must have been the Preparation Committee.

00:12:01.380 --> 00:12:02.280
What is it?

00:12:02.650 --> 00:12:04.180
It's okay if you haven't heard yet.

00:12:04.180 --> 00:12:07.720
How should I say this? I'm sure it's going to be tough, but hang in there.

00:12:08.510 --> 00:12:09.660
Thanks.

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:14.440
Hey, I heard you won the Comifes drawing.

00:12:15.940 --> 00:12:18.300
<i>So that's what he meant...</i>

00:12:18.640 --> 00:12:22.230
Didn't you graduate, Haraguchi-san?

00:12:22.230 --> 00:12:25.550
Yeah, but I stop by every now and then.

00:12:26.820 --> 00:12:27.560
Thanks.

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:30.400
How are things going in Genshiken?

00:12:30.870 --> 00:12:34.910
How, you ask? There's nothing
worth mentioning.

00:12:34.910 --> 00:12:40.110
What's this? Looks like you've got some new members for once.

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:41.820
Hello.

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:48.640
Well, I have some good news to tell you.

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:52.660
I'm in a position to introduce you to many renowned doujin artists,

00:12:52.660 --> 00:12:56.380
so why don't you ask them to write a Kujiun book for you?

00:12:57.230 --> 00:13:01.650
In other words, I'm offering you a chance to make a Kujiun book for the Comifes.

00:13:02.040 --> 00:13:04.510
What do you mean by introduce?

00:13:04.870 --> 00:13:08.140
Well, it'll probably be a page or two per artist.

00:13:08.490 --> 00:13:11.600
The list includes Saibouzu, Kazamatsuri Neko,

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:14.200
Ranmaru Roman, and I'm sure you've heard of Hari Yousuke, haven't you?

00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:16.500
He recently drew the key animation scenes in <i>Halloween Monster</i>.

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:19.900
I can also contact Okegami Ataru and Bellflat Mirai.

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:24.870
Hey, those are all big names. There was even a commercial artist or two in that list.

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:26.490
They're the best of the best, too.

00:13:26.970 --> 00:13:32.760
Well, if you let me handle the management, I can secure at least ten artists, so that's already fifteen pages.

00:13:32.760 --> 00:13:37.400
Kugayama can take care of the rest, so that puts us at 24-pages after we add an index and a colophon.

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:40.480
With the quality and quantity of the names involved,
we can sell each copy for 1,000 yen.

00:13:40.480 --> 00:13:41.240
1,000 yen?

00:13:41.240 --> 00:13:44.500
If we advertise on the Internet
and put some effort into solicitation,

00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:46.090
we could sell around three thousand copies.

00:13:46.090 --> 00:13:48.800
Use simple math and you'll see it adds up to three million.

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:51.510
<i>Three million?</i>

00:13:57.650 --> 00:14:02.080
U-Um, Haraguchi-san, about that...

00:14:02.080 --> 00:14:05.940
Since this is our first time, we'd like to handle everything ourselves.

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:07.780
There's no way that'll sell.

00:14:08.400 --> 00:14:13.990
It's depressing to see that many unsold copies. You have to stand in line just to send it back by courier, too.

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:17.360
Doesn't that sound pathetic?
Besides, the lines hardly move at all.

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:21.950
The most important factor that
determines sales is the artist's name,

00:14:21.950 --> 00:14:23.960
but I'm sure you knew something that obvious.

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:27.460
In order to secure those names,
you need a producer and connections.

00:14:27.770 --> 00:14:34.000
Speaking of which, a girl working at a maid cafe I frequent said she was a big fan of Kazamatsuri Neko.

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:36.490
She's a really cute girl, you know.

00:14:36.490 --> 00:14:40.490
She's the cute otaku type, just like Pyoko-tan and Momokawa Chiaki.

00:14:40.490 --> 00:14:43.380
She's not some pathetic, would-be voice actress.

00:14:43.380 --> 00:14:48.340
I wanted to surprise her, so I brought Kazamatsuri Neko to the cafe,

00:14:48.340 --> 00:14:51.140
since he likes maids, too.

00:14:51.140 --> 00:14:54.820
When I introduced them to each other, she was
so moved, it brought tears to her eyes.

00:14:54.820 --> 00:14:56.990
The sight of that made me teary-eyed, too.

00:14:56.990 --> 00:14:58.830
<i>Should I say it?
Yeah, I did a great thing.</i>

00:14:59.260 --> 00:15:00.320
No.

00:15:00.890 --> 00:15:02.750
Um, Haraguchi-san.

00:15:03.770 --> 00:15:06.470
To tell you the truth, it doesn't have to sell.

00:15:06.470 --> 00:15:08.050
That's basically masturbation.

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:10.030
Are you trying to denounce the virtues of commercialism?

00:15:10.030 --> 00:15:11.780
You won't become an adult that way.

00:15:11.780 --> 00:15:13.420
Isn't it about time you threw your virginity away?

00:15:13.420 --> 00:15:15.340
Throw your virginity away.

00:15:15.340 --> 00:15:19.320
If you keep masturbating for the rest of your life, you'll lose out on half of its greatest pleasure.

00:15:19.320 --> 00:15:21.540
Experience a new sensation.

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:23.570
Selling something feels great.

00:15:24.960 --> 00:15:28.310
Well, I can't really do much about that, can I?

00:15:28.310 --> 00:15:29.650
I'm a virgin after all!

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:31.480
My, you've become hysterical.

00:15:31.480 --> 00:15:33.970
Yes, I've become hysterical!

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:39.610
Yeah, I really have. Give me a break, Haraguchi-san!

00:15:39.610 --> 00:15:43.280
Besides, who are you to tell me when I should throw my virginity away?

00:15:43.280 --> 00:15:45.400
Let us decide that on our own!

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:48.340
Are you sure? Still...

00:15:50.560 --> 00:15:54.430
I already received the consent of everyone I told you about.

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:57.390
<i>What the hell are you doing?</i>

00:15:57.800 --> 00:16:01.620
Very well. I'll personally call everyone and let them know.

00:16:01.620 --> 00:16:04.090
Give me their contact information.

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:09.550
Madarame,

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:12.260
is this okay with you?

00:16:14.590 --> 00:16:18.700
Well, that's what the new president has decided, so cut him some slack.

00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:24.500
Understood. I'll give you their contact information later.

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:26.880
Take care of everything. Bye-bye!

00:16:32.850 --> 00:16:34.750
You did well, Sasayan.

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:37.720
It didn't sound like you had much confidence,

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:41.790
but the way you refused to back down was pretty mature of you.

00:16:41.790 --> 00:16:43.290
It fit the image of a president.

00:16:43.830 --> 00:16:45.840
No, that took a lot out of me.

00:16:45.840 --> 00:16:47.260
Damn that guy.

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:50.510
People like him actually existed, huh?

00:16:51.540 --> 00:16:53.910
The stereotypically offensive type of otaku.

00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:55.630
I hate those types.

00:16:57.050 --> 00:16:59.450
How do you feel about the Sasayan archetype?

00:17:01.140 --> 00:17:03.030
What are you trying to make me say?

00:17:03.490 --> 00:17:05.990
You're the one who classified otakus into types.

00:17:05.990 --> 00:17:08.670
An otaku is an otaku, regardless of the type!

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:09.410
I hate all of them.

00:17:09.820 --> 00:17:11.860
Is that so?

00:17:12.410 --> 00:17:14.040
I guess it can't be helped,

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:16.620
since Sasayan doesn't have any previous experience.

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:18.640
That's enough.

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:23.770
I hate those kinds of jokes, regardless of whether they have to do with otakus or not.

00:17:30.780 --> 00:17:33.880
That should be everyone.

00:17:35.410 --> 00:17:36.830
I'm sorry.

00:17:36.830 --> 00:17:38.450
Don't worry about it.

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:41.240
Have you come up with a title?

00:17:41.760 --> 00:17:44.450
We're thinking about "Iroha Gokko".

00:17:44.950 --> 00:17:45.900
How lame.

00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:49.030
A title is supposed to represent a book's essence, you know.

00:17:49.690 --> 00:17:53.580
Then again, you guys are from Genshiken,
so I guess that's all right.

00:17:53.580 --> 00:17:55.030
Do your best.

00:17:55.030 --> 00:17:56.840
See you later.

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:14.150
U-Um... My name is Sasahara, president of the Society for
the Study of Modern Visual Culture, from Shiiou University.

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:15.170
<i>Shiiou?</i>

00:18:15.170 --> 00:18:16.760
Yes, from Genshiken.

00:18:16.760 --> 00:18:18.870
<i>Oh, Haraguuro's thing?</i>

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:21.630
Yes, yes. Haraguchi-san.

00:18:21.630 --> 00:18:24.060
<i>Sorry, but I haven't started it yet.</i>

00:18:24.420 --> 00:18:29.280
Oh, no. Um, I mean... about that...

00:18:29.280 --> 00:18:30.430
<i>Yeah?</i>

00:18:30.430 --> 00:18:35.350
Haraguchi-san just told us about it a little while ago, so we're not really prepared.

00:18:35.350 --> 00:18:38.120
I'm really sorry, but...

00:18:39.250 --> 00:18:41.900
<i>I bet Haraguuro decided everything on his own.</i>

00:18:42.440 --> 00:18:43.910
Well, that's...

00:18:43.910 --> 00:18:45.430
<i>Am I wrong?</i>

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:47.120
No, you're right, but...

00:18:47.120 --> 00:18:48.950
<i>As I thought.</i>

00:18:48.950 --> 00:18:52.600
<i>We were talking about how typical it was of him to do something like that.</i>

00:18:52.600 --> 00:18:58.720
<i>Taking over his underclassmen's circle, making them pay
for the printing fees, and reaping the profit for himself.</i>

00:18:58.720 --> 00:19:00.930
<i>It looks like he's still up to his dirty old tricks.</i>

00:19:01.810 --> 00:19:04.980
<i>Do whatever you want.
It'll definitely turn out better that way.</i>

00:19:04.980 --> 00:19:06.330
Th-Thank you very much.

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:07.660
What a relief.

00:19:09.820 --> 00:19:12.400
<i>Did you call the others yet?</i>

00:19:12.400 --> 00:19:14.880
No, but I'm going to.

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:18.800
<i>I'm sure everything will go smoothly since everyone hates Haraguuro.</i>

00:19:23.650 --> 00:19:27.900
Saibouzu-san told me that
everything would go smoothly.

00:19:27.900 --> 00:19:29.050
<i>I thought so.</i>

00:19:30.460 --> 00:19:35.060
<i>There are places that need people like him, though.</i>

00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:42.020
<i>If this was a real project, I'm sure three thousand copies
at a thousand yen each would be within reach,</i>

00:19:42.020 --> 00:19:44.020
<i>although it might sound strange hearing that from us.</i>

00:19:44.020 --> 00:19:45.080
Not at all.

00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:49.290
<i>It wouldn't be absurd to think someone could make three million yen in a day.</i>

00:19:50.470 --> 00:19:54.040
<i>Nobody would need to put in extra effort, but
the figures would turn out that way in the end.</i>

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:57.460
<i>The amount that Haraguuro would compensate you guys is another issue entirely, though.</i>

00:19:57.960 --> 00:20:03.780
<i>People who can do what he does without a sense of guilt or shame are few and far between.</i>

00:20:03.780 --> 00:20:04.630
I see...

00:20:04.630 --> 00:20:07.720
<i>Not to say I'd want to be involved with him.</i>

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:12.460
<i>No matter how much of a profit he makes, he'd only
treat us out to dinner once and that'd be the end of it.</i>

00:20:17.310 --> 00:20:19.740
<i>Feel free to call if you need anything else.</i>

00:20:19.740 --> 00:20:21.660
<i>You'll probably get the answering machine most of the time, though.</i>

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:23.860
Okay, excuse me.

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:37.040
<i>Guilt and shame, huh?</i>

00:20:40.490 --> 00:20:47.890
The deadline will be the 27th. We'll print 200 copies of a twenty-four page Kujiun book at the price of 500 yen.

00:20:47.890 --> 00:20:52.400
If we go with those numbers, the printing cost will be sixty thousand yen, which is within our budget.

00:20:52.400 --> 00:20:55.750
Even if we don't manage to sell everything, we'll be able to bring back what's left by ourselves.

00:20:55.750 --> 00:20:58.650
If we sell out, we'll make forty thousand yen.

00:20:59.840 --> 00:21:02.390
Well, that's a number that fits us.

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:04.570
S-Sounds great.

00:21:05.350 --> 00:21:08.990
Let's give it everything we've got for the remaining month.

00:21:10.140 --> 00:21:15.040
<i>That's how our Society for the Study of
Modern Visual Culture, for the first time in years...</i>

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:18.580
<i>for the first time in over a decade, attempted to make a doujinshi.</i>

00:22:54.770 --> 00:22:57.440
Stacking this amount should be
around a hundred copies, I think.

00:22:57.440 --> 00:22:59.700
We definitely want at least two hundred.

00:22:59.700 --> 00:23:00.540
It won't look impressive unless we have at least this many.

00:23:00.540 --> 00:23:02.500
I hope it sells.

00:23:02.500 --> 00:23:03.080
Do you think we need to make point of purchase displays to help us stand out?

00:23:03.080 --> 00:23:05.150
Shouldn't you finish making the book before you get caught up with that?

00:23:05.150 --> 00:23:08.450
Yeah. The conspicuous appearance is an important aspect.

00:23:08.450 --> 00:23:09.490
Right, right, right.

00:23:10.740 --> 00:23:14.990
There have been a lot of titles featuring
"second series" or "season two" in their names lately.

00:23:14.990 --> 00:23:18.140
Right. From a sponsor's perspective,
they can mitigate investment risks.

00:23:18.140 --> 00:23:22.000
From the production team's perspective, they're given more than enough time to schedule everything.

00:23:22.000 --> 00:23:24.390
Instead of airing twenty-six episodes
for two consecutive seasons,

00:23:24.390 --> 00:23:27.960
it's more advantageous to schedule a hiatus of six months to one year.

00:23:27.960 --> 00:23:34.390
What about a show that had a finished source of adaptation and its first season ended two years and nine months ago?

00:23:34.390 --> 00:23:38.000
That's what you call
"being subject to unforeseen circumstances".

00:23:38.000 --> 00:23:39.960
I hope everything goes well.
